Noto Sans SC (the Simplified Chinese page)
  Copyright 2014-2021 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/), with Reserved Font Name
  'Source'.
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 - full text in LICENSE.Noto

  NotoSansSC-Regular.woff2 and NotoSansSC-Bold.woff2 (221,164 bytes together)
  draw the Chinese characters of docs/zh_CN/list_of_commands.html, and of the
  language switch on docs/list_of_commands.html. fonts_zh_CN.css adds them to the
  pages' 'Noto Sans' family by unicode-range, so a browser takes Chinese
  characters from them and everything else from fonts.css; each is fetched only
  when one of its characters is drawn.

  They are Modified Versions under the OFL: the application's own Noto Sans SC
  files (src/resources/fonts/desktop/noto/NotoSansSC/, themselves the Regular
  and Bold instances of Google Fonts' NotoSansSC[wght].ttf 2.004-H2, cut down to
  GB2312; see src/resources/fonts/desktop/README.md and src/resources/fonts/
  LICENSE.fonts for that source and its hashes), cut down again to exactly the
  Chinese characters the pages use, without hinting, and packed as WOFF2.
  They keep the name Noto Sans SC, which does not use the Reserved Font Name,
  and the original's copyright, trademark and licence records (name table).

  SHA-256:
  17e4c2c59a5a217eb4c6d9d990c15819ba8280dd28bdd564f53b07d14f2be577  NotoSansSC-Bold.woff2
  08d2c2b8ca2bb9e8d603240794da840822eb08e9443ad3acf98699a7f9fe01f5  NotoSansSC-Regular.woff2

  To make them again after the Chinese text changes, run these from the project
  folder with fontTools and brotli (the project's .venv has both); the same
  commands give the files above byte for byte. The first lists the characters
  the pages draw from these files (see Docs_Translation.py), the others cut the
  two faces. Then update the SHA-256 lines here: tests/test_docs_translation.py
  fails while a page has a character the files lack, or these lines name other
  files.

    python docs/Docs_Translation.py characters --out characters.txt
    pyftsubset src/resources/fonts/desktop/noto/NotoSansSC/NotoSansSC-Regular.ttf --text-file=characters.txt --flavor=woff2 --no-hinting --name-IDs="*" --notdef-outline --no-recalc-timestamp --recalc-bounds --canonical-order --layout-features="locl,kern,ccmp,mark,mkmk" --output-file=docs/fonts/NotoSansSC-Regular.woff2
    pyftsubset src/resources/fonts/desktop/noto/NotoSansSC/NotoSansSC-Bold.ttf --text-file=characters.txt --flavor=woff2 --no-hinting --name-IDs="*" --notdef-outline --no-recalc-timestamp --recalc-bounds --canonical-order --layout-features="locl,kern,ccmp,mark,mkmk" --output-file=docs/fonts/NotoSansSC-Bold.woff2

The 4,908,576-byte desktop Noto core is not duplicated here. It is stored only
under src/resources/fonts/desktop/ and is registered privately by Qt.
